  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Lovaza / Vascepa approval criteria effective 2021-03-15. Clinical evidence, cautions, duration and quantity require manual review.",
    "CV approval criteria require TG >150 mg/dL; the FDA indications background says ≥150 mg/dL. The approval threshold is encoded.",
    "Use caution with known fish and/or shellfish hypersensitivity.",
    "May cause more frequent symptomatic atrial fibrillation or flutter recurrences in patients with paroxysmal or persistent atrial fibrillation, particularly during the first months of therapy.",
    "Vascepa is associated with increased bleeding risk, greater with concomitant antithrombotics such as aspirin, clopidogrel or warfarin.",
    "Initial approval: up to 3 months. Reauthorization approval: up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity limit: 120 capsules per 30 days; not enforced by predicates."
  ],
